# Blocklist — unit-distance-plane-chromatic
#
# PLAINTEXT. Host-side only. This file is never mounted into the container;
# `scripts/compile-screen` turns it into two artifacts:
#
#   evals/.build/<slug>/screen.json  — mounted read-only into the agent
#                                      container. Every term appears only as a
#                                      salted hash, because `execute_command`
#                                      can read any file the runtime can, and a
#                                      plaintext blocklist would hand the run
#                                      the names it is meant to withhold.
#   evals/.build/<slug>/proxy.deny   — mounted into the proxy container only,
#                                      which the agent cannot read, so hosts
#                                      stay plaintext there.
#
# Terms are normalised (lowercased, diacritics folded, non-alphanumerics
# collapsed to single spaces) and matched as token n-grams, so `de Grey`
# matches `Aubrey D. N. J. de Grey`.
#
#   [block]      a match denies the text outright.
#   [flag]       a match does not deny; it forces the text to the adjudicator
#                and records a ledger entry. For terms too common to block.
#   [host.deny]  never reachable, enforced at the proxy.
#
# Note what is deliberately NOT denied: arxiv.org and the scholarly indexes stay
# reachable. PDFs are text-extracted before the screen sees them, so the paper
# that contains the answer is withheld by its content while the pre-2018
# literature around it stays available. Withholding the venue would test a
# different and less interesting harness.

salt = 7c1f4a9e2b6d80351ea4c7f9b2360d84

[block]

# The solver and the paper
de Grey
Aubrey de Grey
chromatic number of the plane is at least 5
chromatic number of the plane is at least five
1804.02385

# The name of the problem. Not the name of the calibration graph: see below.
Hadwiger Nelson

# The follow-up programme
Polymath16
Polymath 16
Jaan Parts

# The result, described rather than named
1581 vertex unit distance
1345 vertex graph
509 vertex unit distance
five chromatic unit distance graph
5 chromatic unit distance graph
non 4 colourable unit distance graph
non 4 colorable unit distance graph
unit distance graph with chromatic number 5
chromatic number of the plane is 5
chromatic number of the plane at least five

[flag]

# `Moser spindle` was in [block] and that was over-blocking. It is the name of
# the 7-vertex graph the seed asks the run to build, and of **spindling**, a
# 1961 construction technique the seed's own leads section points at. Blocking
# it stopped a live run researching a lead it had been given, which degrades the
# research capability being measured rather than withholding the answer. Flagged
# instead, so the adjudicator can pass a paper about the construction and refuse
# one that announces the 2018 result.
Moser spindle
spindling unit distance

# Individually innocuous, jointly revealing. These escalate to the adjudicator
# rather than denying, because each has legitimate uses in this problem.
1581
1345
509
chromatic number of the plane
Minkowski sum unit distance chromatic
Isbell
Soifer
mathematical coloring book
Geombinatorics

[host.deny]

# The encyclopedia and Q&A tier, where a solved problem's answer is stated as a
# bare fact in the first paragraph. Cheap to withhold and nothing is lost:
# these are not primary sources, and CLAUDE.md already prefers primary ones.
en.wikipedia.org
en.m.wikipedia.org
simple.wikipedia.org
mathworld.wolfram.com
math.stackexchange.com
mathoverflow.net
stackoverflow.com
www.quantamagazine.org
quantamagazine.org

# The specific write-ups of this specific result.
dustingmixon.wordpress.com
terrytao.wordpress.com
michaelnielsen.org
asone.ai
